allers to strip timestamps, normalize absolute paths, or handle other known acceptable differences.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Primary source file is difftest.go, not testutils.go -- named after the primary exported type DiffTest per project file naming convention.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Reference binaries are Homebrew GNU g-prefixed binaries (e.g., gwc, gcat, gls) per architecture design decision DD4. The caller provides the reference binary path; RunDiffTests does not resolve it.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"RunDiffTests prepends LC_ALL=C to the environment for both binaries per architecture design decision DD6, ensuring locale-independent output comparison.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/testutils/difftest.go exists and compiles -- go build ./pkg/testutils/... succeeds with no errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"DiffTest struct is exported with fields for Name, Args, Stdin, and Env\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"RunDiffTests is exported and accepts *testing.T, Go binary path, reference binary path, normalization functions, and []DiffTest\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"On stdout/stderr/exit-code divergence, t.Errorf is called with test name, input args, expected output, and actual output\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Normalization functions are applied to both stdout and stderr before comparison\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/testutils/... reports no issues\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":35080,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"419d195f-4c03-42e4-bd87-0ef4db89e282","uuid":"0efd631b-4fcb-4ccc-ac4c-ec4581a77cd7"}
