e data structures section for the DiffTest struct definition, and design decisions DD2, DD4, and DD6)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-00.0.yaml (test suite for release 00.0 -- read the testutils section for expected test case structure and inputs)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/ (list this directory and read the use case file for testutils)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (list this directory and read the PRD file whose name contains \"testutils\")\n      - go.mod (module path and Go version)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: DiffTest struct, NormalizeFn type alias, RunDiffTests function, binary execution and output comparison logic\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define and export a DiffTest struct with fields for: a descriptive test name (string), command-line arguments ([]string), standard input content (string), and environment variables ([]string). This struct represents a single differential test case per the ARCHITECTURE.yaml data structures definition.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement and export a RunDiffTests function that accepts a *testing.T, the path to the Go binary under test, the path to the reference GNU binary, an optional slice of normalization functions, and a slice of DiffTest cases. For each test case, execute both binaries with identical arguments, stdin, and environment.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Compare stdout, stderr, and exit code between the Go binary and the reference binary for each test case. On any divergence, fail the test using t.Errorf and report: the test case name, the input arguments, the expected output from the reference binary, and the actual output from the Go binary.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Support normalization hooks -- caller-provided functions with signature func([]byte) []byte -- that transform stdout and stderr content before comparison. This enables callers to strip timestamps, normalize absolute paths, or handle other known acceptable differences.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Primary source file is difftest.go, not testutils.go -- named after the primary exported type DiffTest per project file naming convention.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Reference binaries are Homebrew GNU g-prefixed binaries (e.g., gwc, gcat, gls) per architecture design decision DD4. The caller provides the reference binary path; RunDiffTests does not resolve it.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"RunDiffTests prepends LC_ALL=C to the environment for both binaries per architecture design decision DD6, ensuring locale-independent output comparison.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/testutils/difftest.go exists and compiles -- go build ./pkg/testutils/... succeeds with no errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"DiffTest struct is exported with fields for Name, Args, Stdin, and Env\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"RunDiffTests is exported and accepts *testing.T, Go binary path, reference binary path, normalization functions, and []DiffTest\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"On stdout/stderr/exit-code divergence, t.Errorf is called with test name, input args, expected output, and actual output\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Normalization functions are applied to both stdout and stderr before comparison\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/testutils/... reports no issues\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"419d195f-4c03-42e4-bd87-0ef4db89e282","total_cost_usd":0.3955,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":35080,"output_tokens":15118,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15118,"cacheReadInputT